TITLE:: ToggleSwitch
summary:: A nice little Toggle switch
categories:: Undocumented classes
related:: Classes/SomeRelatedClass, Reference/SomeRelatedStuff, etc.

DESCRIPTION::
A horizontal or vertical toggle switch with a label


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
create a new ToggleSwitch.

ARGUMENT:: parent
A parent view.

ARGUMENT:: bounds
A Rect. if width>height, a horizontal switch, otherwise vertical.

ARGUMENT:: label
A label text. For vertical swiches omit or make very short.

ARGUMENT:: toggleSize
The size of the toggle widget (width or height).

ARGUMENT:: label2
An optional second label on the other side of the switch.

ARGUMENT:: radius
a radius size for corners. defualts to \auto .

returns:: a new ToggleSwitch

METHOD:: newSquare
a convencienc method to create a ToggleSwitch with no rouding or button inset.


SECTION::Customizing
All draw function in the class or separated into pr_myMethod methods.

So you can override the methods to add in icon, e.g., if you like.

SECTION::EXAMPLES
Execute the code below to test all the features and parameters.

code::
// basic vertical an horiontal
(
FlowView.new.flow{|w|
	w.parent.background=Color.white;
	w.startRow;
	w.startRow;
	t=ToggleSwitch(w, Rect(0,0,150,18),"Toggle Me").action_({|v| v.value.postln});
		w.startRow;
	r=ToggleSwitch(w, Rect(0,0,18,60),"ff").action_({|v| v.value.postln});


}
)


t.valueAction=1 // turn on

t.onColor_(Color.red(0.8)).refresh // set on color

t.offColor_(Color.green(0.8)).refresh // set off color

t.valueAction=0 // turn off

// two labels , square variant
(
FlowView.new.flow{|w|
	w.parent.background=Color.white;
		t=ToggleSwitch(w, Rect(0,0,150,18),"on",30,"off").action_({|v| v.value.postln});
		w.startRow;
		t=ToggleSwitch.newSquare(w, Rect(0,0,150,18),"off1",36,"on2");
		w.startRow;
		r=ToggleSwitch(w, Rect(0,0,18,80),"ff",36,"cc").action_({|v| v.value.postln});
		w.startRow;
		r=ToggleSwitch.newSquare(w, Rect(0,0,18,80),"ff",36,"cc").action_({|v| v.value.postln}).background_(Color.grey.alpha_(0.1));


}
)

// a dip switches
(
FlowView.new.flow{|w|
			var switches=[];
			var n=8;
			var bounds = Rect(0,0,120,60);

				n.do{|k|
					switches = switches.add(ToggleSwitch(w, Rect(0,0,bounds.width/n,bounds.height),k.asString,35));
				};
		w.startRow;
		bounds = Rect(0,0,60,120);
				n.do{|k|
					switches = switches.add(ToggleSwitch.newSquare(w, Rect(0,0,bounds.width,bounds.height/n),k.asString,35));
				w.startRow;
				};


};
)



